0..77 Comment "//! This fixture migrates thunks from a seat to an operator. Each declaration"
78..139 Comment "//! forms a thunk at the seat and returns it to the operator."
140..143 Comment "//!"
144..223 Comment "//! A thunk crosses with its image. The image holds what the thunk captures and"
224..302 Comment "//! the declarations homed at its world that it names. A thunk is code over an"
303..382 Comment "//! environment. The environment crosses with the code. So a thunk crosses when"
383..451 Comment "//! every capture and every homed declaration that it names crosses."
452..455 Comment "//!"
456..536 Comment "//! The seat reads the image where it forms the thunk. A thunk that the operator"
537..616 Comment "//! forces or applies runs as it runs in place. The three axes of the image are"
617..694 Comment "//! the capture rules. So every capture stands at no region, at ω and at the"
695..717 Comment "//! thunk\'s own world."
718..721 Comment "//!"
722..765 Comment "//! Limits: no former marks a mobile thunk."
766..769 Comment "//!"
770..826 Comment "//! - cites: [Epstein-2011-towards_haskell_in_the_cloud]"
827..830 Comment "//!"
831..983 Comment "//! [Epstein-2011-towards_haskell_in_the_cloud]: https://doi.org/10.1145/2034675.2034690 \"Epstein, Black and Peyton Jones, Towards Haskell in the Cloud\""
985..1063 Comment "// The operator and seat worlds define the exchange. The signature of the seat"
1064..1115 Comment "// seals its side and marks only its report mobile."
